 people. Revenue per employee of $334K ranks in the bottom quartile among Financial Services peers, improving at 16%/yr \u2014 growing workforce leverage. Stock-based compensation of $8K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 8\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["Seacoast Banking Corporation of is a mid-cap financial services business with a $3.2B market cap on $653M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +15% over the past three years and +16% annually across the full decade, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at 7% against a 9% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin 0.7\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield of 2.4% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 92% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.9229295917561195},{"text":"Altman Z in the distress zone (0.2) \u2014 the kind of balance-sheet risk that can make a loss permanent","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 6.6% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are overwhelmingly selling (100% sell ratio) \u2014 the people who know the business want less of it","sev":"amber","cat":"insider","ratio":0.0},{"text":"Above-average market volatility (VIX 26)","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Late-cycle dynamics increase the probability of a slowdown","sev":"amber","cat":"macro"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Seacoast Banking reports Q3 results (SBCF:NASDAQ)","source":"seekingalpha.com","link":"https://seekingalpha.com/news/4666227-seacoast-banking-reports-q3-results","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793863084.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.71,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings"]},{"title":"Seacoast Banking CFO Tracey Dexter Executes 300 SBCF Stock Options at $31.15 Each","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/seacoast-banking-cfo-tracey-dexter-executes-300-sbcf-stock-options-at-3115-each","date":"2026-11-05","timestamp":1793853886.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["leadership"]},{"title":"Trading Systems Reacting to (SBCF) Volatility","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/20/Trading_Systems_Reacting_to_SBCF_Volatility_110326111802_1793722682.html","date":"2026-11-03","timestamp":1793722682.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"SBCF Q3 deep dive: margin outlook improves as 